From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5sd <ps5sd@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] server: ggml's "insufficient memory" is out of memory

When the CPU heap runs out inside ggml's own C code, ggml logs
"ggml_aligned_malloc: insufficient memory" before it asserts. PS5SD turns
that assertion into std::bad_alloc (its abort callback), so the run fails
instead of the title; but the failure log did not take the line as a memory
failure, and the run failed as generation_failed with ggml's text. It is one
of the memory markers now: the run gets its one more try (0072), and fails
as out_of_memory with the message that says what to lower.

diff --git a/examples/server/server_hooks.cpp b/examples/server/server_hooks.cpp
index d0c6abb..7724df2 100644
--- a/examples/server/server_hooks.cpp
+++ b/examples/server/server_hooks.cpp
@@ -130,6 +130,9 @@ bool memory_line_locked() {
         "outofdevicememory",
         "outofhostmemory",
         "failed to allocate",
+        // ggml_aligned_malloc, when the CPU heap is out (PS5SD: the app's abort callback
+        // then ends the run instead of the process)
+        "insufficient memory",
     };
     for (const FailureLine& line : g_failure_lines) {
         for (const char* marker : k_memory_markers) {
